/*
# Load real Delhi-NCR hospital dataset (final part)

1. Purpose
- Replaces the generic placeholder hospital rows with the 20 real Delhi-NCR hospitals
  (AIIMS, Safdarjung, RML, LNJP, GTB, Sir Ganga Ram, Medanta, Apollo, etc.) including
  simulated capacity data in the `raw` JSONB column: ICU beds, ventilators, equipment,
  clinical capabilities (24x7 / day-only / none) and medical stock (ASV, anti-rabies,
  adrenaline, thrombolysis, oxygen).

2. Tables modified
- `staff_users`: hospital_id temporarily set to NULL (re-pointed to new rows at the end).
- `hospitals`: all rows replaced with the 20 real hospitals, real addresses/cities,
  approximate real coordinates, and the `raw` capabilities/stock JSONB.
- `queue_entries`, `emergency_requests`, `transfer_requests`, `transfer_legs`, `asv_stock`:
  demo rows referencing the old placeholder hospitals are cleared.
- `asv_stock` re-seeded from each hospital's raw.resources.asv quantity.

3. Security
- No changes to RLS or policies. The existing public-read policy for hospitals continues
  to serve the hospital list to the app.

4. Notes
- All capacity/stock numbers are SIMULATED demo data (flagged in raw.data_status).
- Staff accounts are re-linked to new hospital rows (admin1 → AIIMS, doctor1/reception1 →
  Safdarjung) so the staff dashboards keep working.
*/

UPDATE staff_users SET hospital_id = NULL;

DELETE FROM asv_stock;
DELETE FROM transfer_legs;
DELETE FROM transfer_requests;
DELETE FROM emergency_requests;
DELETE FROM queue_entries;

DELETE FROM hospitals;

